  "tool": "linode_audit_summary",
  "description": "CapMeta audit aggregator (no Linode API call). The seeded audit_store fixes the window, so the bucket rows and their counts are a shared contract; group_by drives which columns the rows carry. The status case puts two events in one bucket, which is what makes the counting itself observable: a bucket every event lands in alone cannot tell a count from a constant. The SQLite case seeds only the database, so the same rows coming back prove the aggregator read the store the config named rather than the log beside it. The refusal case names a column the vocabulary does not carry: its whole sentence is declared on AuditSummaryInput, so one contract edit moves both languages and this case is what notices.",
